{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"NJ Anti-Eviction Act criminal-activity eviction causes","requirement":"A landlord may evict where the tenant is convicted of or civilly liable for assault, threats, theft, drug activity or human trafficking on the premises; a 3-day notice to quit is required and suit must be filed within two years.","key_value":"3-day notice to quit; 2-year filing limit","coverage_conditions":"Tenants convicted of or civilly liable for the listed offenses, and tenants who knowingly permit such a person to reside at the premises; juvenile delinquency findings also qualify.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"No suit more than two years after the delinquency finding, conviction or release from incarceration, whichever is later; the civil-liability cause does not apply to a tenant allowing a juvenile found delinquent for drug use or possession to reside there.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"No eviction suit may be brought more than two years after: the juvenile was found to be delinquent; conviction of the person; or after the person’s release from incarceration, whichever is later. A Notice to Quit must be served on the tenant at least three day s prior to filing a suit for (N.J.S.A. 2A-18-61.1(o)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Owner-occupied two- and three-family dwelling eviction causes","requirement":"Tenants of landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings may be removed only by court order for holding over, nonpayment, disorderly conduct, willful damage, rule violations or lease re-entry violations; a three-month, one-month or three-day notice to quit applies according to tenancy type and cause.","key_value":"3-month/1-month/3-day notice to quit","coverage_conditions":"Tenants of landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":2,"max_units":3,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"landlord-occupied two- and three-family dwellings"},"exemptions":"No further notice is required where the tenant stays after failing to pay rent; a three-day notice applies to disorderly, destructive or written-rule-violating causes.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.2","quoted_span":"A three (3) month notice to quit must be gi ven if an at will tenancy or year -to-year tenancy exists. A one (1) month notice to quit is required for a month-to-month tenancy and other types of tenancies are entitled to a one (1) month notice to quit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Rooming and boarding house eviction good cause and notice rules","requirement":"Owners of rooming and boarding houses must follow the Eviction Law's good causes and notice requirements when evicting residents, and must give at least three working days' notice to the County Welfare Board before starting an eviction action.","key_value":"3 working days' notice to County Welfare Board","coverage_conditions":"Buildings with at least two living units occupied by unrelated persons without private kitchens and bathrooms, unless a Rooming and Boarding House Act exception applies.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":2,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"rooming and boarding houses regulated under N.J.A.C. 5:27"},"exemptions":"Hotels with more than 85 percent temporary occupancy by people with homes elsewhere, school and college dormitories, buildings housing only college students, and certain residences for the disabled.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3","quoted_span":"The Regulations Governing Rooming and Boarding Houses, which are enforced by the Bureau of Rooming and Boarding House Standards of the Department of Community Affairs, require owners of rooming and boarding houses to follow the good causes and notice requirements of the Eviction Law when evicting residents, except if otherwise ordered by the Bureau (N.J.A.C. 5:27-3.3(c)). There is a further requirement that the owner give at least three (3) working days’ notice to the County Welfare Board before starting the eviction action for any resident (N.J.A.C. 5:26-3.4(c)).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Penalties for eviction law violations on owner occupancy and demolition","requirement":"A landlord who evicts to personally occupy must occupy at least six months; one who evicts to demolish or permanently retire a building must not use it residentially for five years, facing treble damages, fees and penalties.","key_value":"5-year residential-use bar; treble damages; up to $10,000 penalty","coverage_conditions":"Tenants who vacate after notice that the landlord will personally occupy the unit or will permanently remove the property from residential use.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Three times the damages plus attorney fees and costs; civil penalty up to $10,000.00 per violation; property may not be registered as a planned real estate development for five years.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.6","quoted_span":"If the landlord allows any residential use of the unit during the five (5) year period from the date the unit became vacant, the landlord, or the former landlord, may be liable to the tenant for three (3) times the damages plus attorney fees and costs. Additionally, the landlord or former landlord may be liable for a civil penalty up to $10,000.00 for each violation of this law","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-reprisal protection for tenants exercising civil rights","requirement":"A landlord may not retaliate by eviction, substantial alteration of the lease, or refusal to renew when a tenant enforces lease or legal rights, makes a good-faith complaint to a government authority, joins a tenant organization, or refuses lease changes made in reprisal.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All rental properties used for dwelling purposes, including mobile homes, except owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":null},"exemptions":"Owner-occupied two- or three-family dwellings are excluded.","penalty":"The tenant may sue the landlord for damages in a civil action.","effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot take reprisal action against a tenant by eviction, substantial alteration of a lease or its terms, or refusal to renew a lease when a tenant exercises certain civil rights (N.J.S.A. 2A:42-10.10).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"90-day notice before eviction of tenants after foreclosure","requirement":"Foreclosure alone is not grounds for eviction; a buyer who will personally occupy the property must give a 90-day notice to quit, and new owners must notify tenants in English and Spanish within 10 business days of the sale.","key_value":"90-day notice to quit; 10-business-day notice of sale","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental units in foreclosed properties; month-to-month tenants and owner-occupied two- and three-family units are not exempt from the 90-day notice.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"residential rental units in foreclosed property"},"exemptions":"If the tenant's lease goes beyond the 90 days, no eviction until the lease expires and the 90-day notice is given; the notice may be given 90 days before the lease expires.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:50-69","quoted_span":"Before a tenant can be evicted due to foreclosure, the landlord must provide the tenant with a 90 -day notice to qui t when the foreclosed property has been purchased by a buyer who wants to personally occupy it as his or her primary residence.","interaction":"Federal law does not preempt State or local laws that provide longer time periods or other additional protections for tenants in foreclosure proceedings.","confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act","requirement":"Eligible senior, disabled or disabled-veteran tenants who lived in a building being converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership at least one year before the conversion recording may be protected from eviction for 40 years if family income is within the limit.","key_value":"40 years' protection; income up to 3x county average per-person income or $50,000, whichever is greater","coverage_conditions":"Tenants at least 62 before the conversion recording date, permanently disabled tenants, or disabled veterans discharged under certain circumstances, who lived in the building at least one year before the conversion recording.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":"Family income must not exceed three times the county average per person income or $50,000, whichever is greater; applications are generally within 60 days, with late filings accepted for good reason if conversion has not occurred.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28","quoted_span":"Tenants may be protected from eviction for 40 years if their family income is not more than three (3) times the average per person income in their county or $50,000.00, whichever  is greater (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.28).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-04","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Tenant Protection Act of 1992 protected tenancy","requirement":"Extends protected-tenancy protections to qualified tenants in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible under the 1981 Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act, in qualified counties; Hudson County is currently the only qualified county.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Qualified tenants in qualified counties, currently only Hudson County, in buildings converted or being converted.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40","quoted_span":"The Tenant Protection Law of 1992 amendment extends protections to qualified tenants in qualified counties in buildings converted or being converted who were not eligible for Protected Tenancy as either Senior Citizens or Disabled Persons under the “Senior Citizens and Disabled Protected Tenancy Act of 1981” (N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.40 to -61.59; N.J.A.C. 5:24-3.1 to -3.4).","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
